window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"tahmkench","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench","Skill","Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 3","text":"Three stacks arrive — spend them on Devour, since the Q stun consumes all three."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"Anti-heal first: Darkin Glaive and Grim Deliverance both heal him on cooldown."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Near-unkillable, but Aureate Rush still scales off your max HP."},{"when":"Grouped fights","text":"Devour his engage; Dreaded Return pulls from 850 range every 14s."}],"wants":{"you":["Three An Acquired Taste stacks","Extended trades your grey health absorbs","Grievous Wounds before his all-in"],"foe":["Kills found before your level 3","Aureate Rush percent-health into your HP","Determination filled so he can revive"]},"early":"Levels 1 and 2 are honest farming — Zaahen has no stun at all, only the Darkin Glaive knockup on its recast. Level 3 hands you the trade game. Stack An Acquired Taste, absorb his aggression, and remember that Aureate Rush deals percent health, so Heartsteel alone will not save you.","mid":"At 6 your R is Devour, a fight-winner and not a map tool — three stacks removes him outright. Watch the displacement race: Abyssal Dive knocks up, his Q recast knocks up and Dreaded Return pulls from 850 every 14s, and whoever lands it first owns the trade. Grim Deliverance heals him too.","late":"At two-plus items you are a near-unkillable brick, with one caveat: Aureate Rush scales off your max health, so stacking HP alone feeds it. Cultivation of War also lets a fully-stacked Zaahen revive, so a won fight is not always over. Sit on his target and soak the burst.","whys":["Level 1 is a skill check with both champions just farming.","Level 2 stays even — his Darkin Glaive recast knockup is the only CC.","Level 3 is yours: bank three stacks, then Devour — the Q stun spends them.","Levels 4-5 even out — Aureate Rush is back every 10s.","Level 6 favours you: Devour is a fight-winner here, not a roam tool.","First item: anti-heal him — both Darkin Glaive and his R heal him.","With 2+ items you win the 1v1 — but a full-stacked Zaahen can revive."]});
